package Libraries.Interface.Controls.Support

use Libraries.Interface.Controls.TextField
use Libraries.Interface.Controls.Spreadsheet
use Libraries.Interface.Events.FocusEvent

/*
The SpreadsheetCellField class is the text field a Spreadsheet places over a
cell while the user edits it in place. Typing, the caret and the selection
work as in any text field. Enter keeps the edit and moves down, Shift-Enter
up, Tab right and Shift-Tab left; Escape cancels. Leaving the field another
way, such as by clicking elsewhere, keeps the edit. Its name for screen
readers is the cell's, such as "Cell C2". Each Spreadsheet makes its own, so
most users won't need this class directly.

Attribute: Author William Allee

Attribute: Example
use Libraries.Interface.Controls.Spreadsheet
use Libraries.Interface.Controls.Support.SpreadsheetCellField
Spreadsheet sheet
SpreadsheetCellField field = sheet:GetEditField()
*/
class SpreadsheetCellField is TextField
    Spreadsheet sheet = undefined

    on create
        SetInputGroup("SpreadsheetCellField")
        SetName("Cell")
    end

    /*
    This action connects the field to its spreadsheet. The Spreadsheet calls
    it.

    Attribute: Parameter sheet The spreadsheet.
    */
    action SetSpreadsheet(Spreadsheet sheet)
        me:sheet = sheet
    end

    /*
    This action returns the field's spreadsheet.

    Attribute: Returns The spreadsheet.
    */
    action GetSpreadsheet returns Spreadsheet
        return sheet
    end

    /*
    This action is called when the field gets the focus. It does what a text
    field does; it is here because the field also overrides LostFocus, and
    TextField's focus actions come from more than one parent.

    Attribute: Parameter event The focus event.
    */
    action GainedFocus(FocusEvent event)
        parent:TextField:GainedFocus(event)
    end

    /*
    This action is called when the field loses the focus. If the spreadsheet
    is still editing, as when the user clicked somewhere else, the edit is
    kept.

    Attribute: Parameter event The focus event.
    */
    action LostFocus(FocusEvent event)
        parent:TextField:LostFocus(event)
        if sheet not= undefined and sheet:IsEditing()
            sheet:CommitEditingWithoutFocus()
        end
    end
end
